# Line-ending and binary-file policy.
#
# Without this file, core.autocrlf=true makes git treat any blob without NUL
# bytes as text. A PNG that happens to contain no NUL byte is then rewritten on
# checkout (every 0x0A becomes 0x0D 0x0A), silently corrupting it. The same risk
# applies to the decks, the PDFs and the Word report. Mark every binary format
# explicitly so the working tree and the blob stay byte-identical.

# --- binaries: never normalise, never diff as text -------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.pptx  binary
*.docx  binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.zip   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary

# --- text: keep the repository's existing normalisation --------------------
*.py        text
*.md        text
*.toml      text
*.yaml      text
*.yml       text
*.json      text
*.cfg       text
*.txt       text
*.html      text
*.css       text
*.js        text
*.svg       text

# Frozen fingerprint fixtures must be byte-identical on every platform; the
# writer already emits LF, and this rule stops a checkout from rewriting it.
tests/fixtures/*.json  text eol=lf
